    {
      "text": "If thou doest well, shalt thou not be accepted, Gen. 4:7. What is this that thou hast done, Gen. 12:18. thou hast done deeds unto me that ought not to be done, Gen. 20:9. whatsoever God hath said unto thee, do, Gen. 31:16. When ye do the office of a midwife, Ex. 1:16. All that the Lord hath spoken we will do, Ex. 19:8. we will hear it, and do it, Deut. 5:27. do according unto all that which is written, 2 Kgs. 22:13. Trust in the Lord, and do good, Ps. 37:3. I delight to do thy will, Ps. 40:8. not fear: what can man do unto me, Ps. 118:6 (Heb. 13:6). Say not, I will do so to him as he hath done to me, Prov. 24:29. Whatsoever thy hand findeth to do, do it with thy might, Eccl. 9:10. hear thy words, but they will not do them, Ezek. 33:31. have spoken it, and I will do it, Ezek. 36:36.",
